  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project aims to develop a database and analysis system for chemical structures. This dataset consists of 328 chemical compounds, each labeled with its half-life for aerobic aqueous biodegradation. The project involves creating a robust system to store, manage, and analyze this data for regression analysis tasks.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to facilitate the analysis of chemical compounds' biodegradability. The system should support efficient storage and retrieval of data, allowing scientists to perform regression tasks to determine patterns or predictions regarding the compounds' biodegradability.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Researchers and scientists interested in chemical analysis and biodegradability.\n- Database administrators managing the chemical data and ensuring data integrity.\n- Developers or data analysts conducting regression analysis and modeling.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system will store detailed chemical structure information across several tables, including atoms, bonds, molecular groups, and molecules.\n- Users can query the database to retrieve information on specific compounds, their atomic structures, and biodegradability statistics.\n- The database will establish relationships between atoms and molecules, as well as groupings of atoms for more complex structures.\n- It will provide facilities to update and maintain the dataset, ensuring accurate and up-to-date information.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system must ensure data integrity through foreign key constraints and cascading updates and deletes.\n- It should support scalability to handle additional data entries as needed.\n- The database performance must be optimized for swift query processing and data retrieval to support user analysis activities.\n- Security measures should be in place to protect sensitive scientific data from unauthorized access.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0094\nCREATE TABLE `molecules` (\n  `molecule_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `compound_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `half_life_hours` decimal(10,4) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`molecule_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `atoms` (\n  `atom_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `molecule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `atom_index` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `element_symbol` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `atomic_number` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `formal_charge` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `x_coord` decimal(12,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `y_coord` decimal(12,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `z_coord` decimal(12,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`atom_id`),\n  KEY `atoms_ibfk_1` (`molecule_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `atoms_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecules` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `bonds` (\n  `bond_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `molecule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `atom1_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `atom2_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bond_order` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bond_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`bond_id`),\n  KEY `bonds_ibfk_1` (`molecule_id`),\n  KEY `bonds_ibfk_2` (`atom1_id`),\n  KEY `bonds_ibfk_3` (`atom2_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `bonds_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecules` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `bonds_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`atom1_id`) REFERENCES `atoms` (`atom_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `bonds_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`atom2_id`) REFERENCES `atoms` (`atom_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `molecular_groups` (\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `molecule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `group_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `group_type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`group_id`),\n  KEY `molecular_groups_ibfk_1` (`molecule_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `molecular_groups_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecules` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `group_atoms` (\n  `group_atom_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `atom_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`group_atom_id`),\n  KEY `group_atoms_ibfk_1` (`group_id`),\n  KEY `group_atoms_ibfk_2` (`atom_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `group_atoms_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `molecular_groups` (`group_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `group_atoms_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`atom_id`) REFERENCES `atoms` (`atom_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
